# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CAUSE OF THE TERM 47 LIVELOCK, isolated 2026-08-01 (churn + components backend):
#
# A growing blocklet (Dn, nursery, cursor pc 6) fails a placement merge, and its
# relief's shift is blocked by the cursor's OWN cell. Two nearby cells then churn
# 22k times while ending EMPTY: a route is pushed out and pulled back forever.
#
# The culprit is not this patch, it is relief_pays. The pays-for-itself exemption
# lets a paid relief DESCEND the displacement order -- but it does so in BOTH
# directions, so two paid placements (or one alternating between attempts) can
# shuttle a single route between them indefinitely. The order was the only thing
# preventing that, and "pays for itself" removes it symmetrically.
#
# Opening the ring does not cause the cycle; it supplies the room for one that the
# exemption already permitted. That is why term 47 fails here and nowhere else, and
# why the doomed-dock fix (named declines) did not touch it.
#
# THE FIX TO TRY FIRST: make the exemption ASYMMETRIC. A paid relief may descend the
# order only when the receiver is strictly further from the requesting placement
# than the source -- the same "drain is a direction" shape this patch applies to the
# ring, applied to the exemption itself. A shuttle needs one leg inward; forbid the
# inward leg and the pair cannot cycle, while the outward leg that actually buys the
# fire stays legal.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
